Hello,

Those of you who have the early GTs with the black and silver 'flower petal' wheels may not know that they have a plastic aero cover installed on them.

While useful for getting maximum range, I much prefer the look of the wheels with the covers removed.

There's only one problem: There is no center cap covering the axle shaft under the aero cover and the wheel is not designed to use a 'standard' center cap.

There are some cheap chinese center cap kits that mostly fit (I used one for about 6 months and it worked okay) but I wanted a better solution that kept the mustang logo on the wheels.

So I designed these adapters that fit into the wheel center bore and allow you to snap the center caps that are installed onto the aero covers into the space that is open when you remove the aero covers.

They are printed out of nylon, the same material as the center caps themselves for strength and heat/UV resistance.

I am thinking of selling these kits. Is there any interest for other owners?
